      "message": "Optional: Do we still need `kMinBytes` here (and this function?), or should the minimum alignment/granularity live in `sk_malloc_good_size`\u0027s contract?\n\n`malloc` already guarantees alignment, and clamping to `kMinBytes` beforehand can bump small requests into the next bucket when an allocator\u0027s smallest slot has `\u003c kMinBytes` of usable space (e.g. due to in-slot metadata) unless this is meant as a floor for embedders that implement `sk_malloc_good_size(s)` as `return s;`?\n\nFor example, in PartitionAlloc with BackupRefPtr enabled (4B in-slot metadata), the 16B slot has 12B of usable capacity, so clamping `\u003c\u003d12B` to `16B` beforehand bumps it into the 32B bucket.",
